/// Chapter 5 of the guide, written from md-docs/learn/03-tutorial-todos.md by
/// scripts/docsite/guide.py; edit the guide, not this file.
page TodosGuide(path: "/docs/tutorials/todos", title: "Tutorial: Todos", description: "A beginner WebFluent tutorial: a todo app with a persisted store, a component, a keyed list, a filter in the address and tests, in 20 minutes.", layout: DocsShell("Tutorial: Todos", chapter: t("nav.group.tutorials"), blurb: "Build a todo list kept in the reader's browser — types, a store that remembers, a component, a filter in the address and tests that click.", source: "md-docs/learn/03-tutorial-todos.md", sections: [Anchor(id: "before-you-start", label: "Before you start"), Anchor(id: "step-1-create-the-project", label: "Step 1: Create the project"), Anchor(id: "step-2-give-it-a-look-of-its-own", label: "Step 2: Give it a look of its own"), Anchor(id: "step-3-describe-a-todo", label: "Step 3: Describe a todo"), Anchor(id: "step-4-write-a-store-that-remembers", label: "Step 4: Write a store that remembers"), Anchor(id: "step-5-build-one-row", label: "Step 5: Build one row"), Anchor(id: "step-6-write-the-page", label: "Step 6: Write the page"), Anchor(id: "step-7-write-tests", label: "Step 7: Write tests"), Anchor(id: "step-8-build-it", label: "Step 8: Build it"), Anchor(id: "what-you-built", label: "What you built")], prevTo: "/docs/guide/coming-from", prevLabel: t("ch.04"), nextTo: "/docs/tutorials/field-notes", nextLabel: t("ch.06"))) {
    Stack(gap: .lg) {
        Markdown("This is the first of three tutorials that each build a whole project, step by step. Each project is complete in the repository under `examples/tutorials/`, and none needs a server: what a project keeps, it keeps in the reader's browser.")

        Table(caption: "Tutorial: Todos") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Tutorial").header
                    Table.Cell("What you build").header
                    Table.Cell("What it teaches").header
                    Table.Cell("Time").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("[Todos](/docs/tutorials/todos)") }
                    Table.Cell("A list of things to do: add, tick, rename, filter")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("Types, a store with `persist`, a component, a keyed list, a filter in the address, tests that click") }
                    Table.Cell("20 minutes")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("[Field Notes](/docs/tutorials/field-notes)") }
                    Table.Cell("A notebook site, statically built, a page per note")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`data` files, a layout, `:slug` pages with `paths:`, Markdown pages, search and tags, what a pre-rendered page can know") }
                    Table.Cell("An hour")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("[Pocket](/docs/tutorials/pocket)") }
                    Table.Cell("A budget tracker with a dashboard, forms and two languages")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`Money` and `Date`, derived totals, a `persist` migration, `validate`, a dialog and shortcuts, i18n and right-to-left text, a script of your own, offline") }
                    Table.Cell("A couple of hours")
                }
            }
        }

        Markdown("If you have not written WebFluent before, start with [the Shelf tutorial](/docs/guide/tutorial): it is a gentler first half hour.\n\n**What you will build.** A list of things to do, kept in the reader's browser: add a todo, tick it, rename it, remove it, and show only the open ones. It is one page, one store and one component. The finished project is [`examples/tutorials/easy-todos`](https://github.com/monzeromer-lab/WebFluent/tree/master/examples/tutorials/easy-todos).\n\n**Time:** about 20 minutes.")

        Heading("Before you start", id: "before-you-start").h2

        Markdown("You need:\n\n- `wf` installed and on your `PATH` — `wf --version` prints `wf 5.11.0` or later ([Getting started](/docs/guide/getting-started)).\n- Chrome or Chromium on the machine, for the tests that click and for `wf verify`. Set `WF_CHROME` to its path when it is not in a usual place.\n- Git, to fetch the finished projects.\n\nEvery code block whose first line names a file — `// src/stores/Todos.wf` — is that file, or a run of lines from it, exactly as the project has it. A test holds this chapter to the projects, so the code you read here is the code that builds.\n\nTo start from a finished project instead, clone the repository and serve one:")

        Terminal(lines: [
                Line(command: "git clone https://github.com/monzeromer-lab/WebFluent"),
                Line(command: "cd WebFluent/examples/tutorials/easy-todos"),
                Line(command: "wf serve")
            ])

        Markdown("**Check it:** the terminal prints `Starting dev server at http://localhost:3000/`, and that address shows the project.\n\nFor this tutorial you need only `wf` and Chrome. You write every file of this project yourself, and the blocks below hold each file whole, except the tests, where one of six is shown.")

        Heading("Step 1: Create the project", id: "step-1-create-the-project").h2

        Markdown("Make a single-page project and go into it:")

        Terminal(lines: [
                Line(command: "wf init todos -t spa"),
                Line(command: "cd todos")
            ])

        Markdown("Delete everything the template put in `src/` and in `tests/`: you write every file yourself, and the template's tests would fail without its pages. Then replace `webfluent.app.json` with this:")

        CodeBlock(#"{
  "name": "todos",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "theme": { "name": "Paper", "dark": "Night" },
  "build": { "output": "./build", "output_type": "spa", "csp": true },
  "meta": {
    "title": "Todos",
    "description": "A small list of things to do, kept in your browser.",
    "lang": "en",
    "favicon": "/favicon.svg"
  }
}"#, title: "json")

        Markdown("- `\"output_type\": \"spa\"` makes a single-page app: one HTML shell, with pages swapped without a reload ([Static sites and SPAs](/docs/guide/static-and-spa)).\n- `\"csp\": true` ships a content security policy and holds the build to it ([Security](/docs/guide/security)).\n- `theme` names two themes, `Paper` and `Night`, which you write in the next step.\n\n**Check it:** `wf check` prints `IO Error: No .wf files found in src/`. That is expected: `src/` is empty until the next step.")

        Heading("Step 2: Give it a look of its own", id: "step-2-give-it-a-look-of-its-own").h2

        Markdown("The config names a theme, so declare it first. A theme names only the design tokens it changes; every other token keeps its default ([Styling](/docs/guide/styling)). `Night` is the theme named as `\"dark\"` in the config, and the page uses it when the reader's system is set to dark:")

        CodeBlock(#"// src/theme.wf
/// Warm paper and ink, with one teal for what you can act on.
theme Paper {
    color-primary: #0F766E
    color-background: #F6F4EF
    color-surface: #FFFFFF
    color-text: #1F2328
    color-text-muted: #5E6670
    color-border: #E4E0D8
    font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif
    radius-md: 10px
}

/// The same page after dark.
theme Night {
    color-primary: #2DD4BF
    color-background: #14171A
    color-surface: #1C2024
    color-text: #ECEEF0
    color-text-muted: #A3ABB3
    color-border: #2C3238
}"#, title: "wf")

        Markdown("The page you write in step 6 names classes — `card`, `todo`, `is-done`, `filters` — and `src/todos.css` styles them. The build bundles every `.css` file under `src/`, so the file needs no link. These are four of its rules; copy the whole file from the [finished project](https://github.com/monzeromer-lab/WebFluent/blob/master/examples/tutorials/easy-todos/src/todos.css):")

        CodeBlock(#".todo { flex-wrap: nowrap; padding: 0.6rem 0.25rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
.todo__title { flex: 1; }
.todo.is-done .todo__title { text-decoration: line-through; color: var(--color-text-muted); }
.filters a.is-on { background: var(--color-background); color: var(--color-text); font-weight: 600; }"#, title: "css")

        Markdown("Each colour is a token, `var(--color-border)`, so the dark theme recolours the page with no rule of its own.\n\n**Check it:** `wf check` prints `No problems in todos.`")

        Heading("Step 3: Describe a todo", id: "step-3-describe-a-todo").h2

        Markdown("A `type` names the fields a value has, and the checker holds every use to them ([Types](/docs/guide/types)). An `enum` is a fixed set of cases:")

        CodeBlock(#"// src/types.wf
/// One thing to do.
type Todo {
    id: Uuid
    title: String
    done: Bool = false
}

/// Which todos the list shows.
enum Filter { all, open, done }"#, title: "wf")

        Markdown("- `Uuid` is one of the types the language brings; `uuid()` makes one.\n- `done` has a default, so a new todo can leave it out.\n- A case is written with a dot, `.open`, wherever a `Filter` is wanted.\n\nBecause the checker knows the fields, `todo.titel` is an error where it is written, and the message names the field you meant.\n\n**Check it:** `wf check` prints `No problems in todos.`")

        Heading("Step 4: Write a store that remembers", id: "step-4-write-a-store-that-remembers").h2

        Markdown("A store holds state that any page or component can read ([Stores](/docs/guide/stores)). This one keeps the list:")

        CodeBlock(#"// src/stores/Todos.wf
/// The list, kept in the browser between visits.
store Todos {
    persist items: [Todo] = []

    derived open = items.filter(todo => !todo.done)
    derived done = items.filter(todo => todo.done)

    action add(title: String) {
        let text = title.trim()
        if text == "" { return }
        items = items.concat([Todo(id: uuid(), title: text)])
    }

    action toggle(id: Uuid) {
        items = items.map(todo => if todo.id == id { { ...todo, done: !todo.done } } else { todo })
    }

    action rename(id: Uuid, title: String) {
        let text = title.trim()
        if text == "" { return }
        items = items.map(todo => if todo.id == id { { ...todo, title: text } } else { todo })
    }

    action remove(id: Uuid) {
        items = items.filter(todo => todo.id != id)
    }

    action clearDone() {
        items = items.filter(todo => !todo.done)
    }
}"#, title: "wf")

        Markdown("- `persist` is a `state` kept in the browser's storage. The list is still there after a reload, and a second tab follows the first, with no storage code written.\n- A `derived` value follows what it reads: `open` is always the todos not yet done.\n- An action is the one place state changes. `\{ ...todo, done: !todo.done \}` is the todo with one field changed.\n- `rename`, `remove` and `clearDone` change the list in the same way.\n\n**Check it:** `wf check` prints seven `U04` warnings, such as ``warning[U04]: `Todos.open` is declared but never read``. That is expected: nothing reads the store yet. The page in step 6 reads every member, and the warnings go.")

        Heading("Step 5: Build one row", id: "step-5-build-one-row").h2

        Markdown("A component is an element of your own ([Components](/docs/guide/components)). This one draws a single todo, and lets the reader rename it in place:")

        CodeBlock(#"// src/components/TodoRow.wf
/// One row of the list: a box to tick, the title, and buttons to rename and
/// remove it.
component TodoRow(_ todo: Todo) {
    use Todos
    state editing = false
    state draft = todo.title

    action save() {
        Todos.rename(todo.id, draft)
        editing = false
    }

    Row(class: ["todo", if todo.done { "is-done" }], align: .center, gap: .sm) {
        Checkbox(checked: todo.done, aria-label: "Done: {todo.title}") {
            on change { Todos.toggle(todo.id) }
        }
        if editing {
            // `mount:` runs when the input is made: the cursor goes straight in.
            Input(bind: draft, aria-label: "New title for {todo.title}", class: "todo__edit", mount: (n) => n.focus()) {
                on key("Enter") { save() }
                on key("Escape") { draft = todo.title  editing = false }
                on blur { save() }
            }
        } else {
            Text(todo.title, class: "todo__title")
            IconButton(icon: "edit", label: "Rename {todo.title}", class: "todo__action").sm {
                on click { draft = todo.title  editing = true }
            }
        }
        IconButton(icon: "trash", label: "Remove {todo.title}", class: "todo__action").sm {
            on click { Todos.remove(todo.id) }
        }
    }
}"#, title: "wf")

        Markdown("- `_ todo` is the component's one positional prop, so a call reads `TodoRow(todo)`.\n- Its `state` belongs to each row: renaming one row does not put the others in edit mode.\n- `class:` adds classes to the element's own. The list form may hold an `if`, which adds `is-done` only while the todo is done.\n- Every control has an accessible name. The checkbox and the icon buttons say which todo they act on, so a screen reader — and the tests in step 7 — can tell them apart ([Accessibility](/docs/guide/accessibility)).\n\n**Check it:** `wf check` prints `U03` for `TodoRow` (nothing places it yet) and four `U04` warnings. The store's `toggle`, `rename` and `remove` no longer appear: the row calls them.")

        Heading("Step 6: Write the page", id: "step-6-write-the-page").h2

        Markdown("The page holds the box for a new todo, the filters and the list. Here is its first half:")

        CodeBlock(#"// src/pages/Home.wf
page Home(path: "/", title: "Todos", description: "A small list of things to do, kept in your browser.") {
    use Todos
    state draft = ""

    // The filter lives in the address — `/?show=open` — so a reload or a
    // shared link keeps it.
    derived filter: Filter = if query.show == "open" { .open } else if query.show == "done" { .done } else { .all }
    derived shown = match filter {
        .open { Todos.open }
        .done { Todos.done }
        .all { Todos.items }
    }

    action add() {
        Todos.add(draft)
        draft = ""
    }

    Stack(class: "card", gap: .md) {
        Row(justify: .between, align: .baseline) {
            Heading("Todos").h1
            Text("{Todos.open.length} left", class: "count")
        }

        Row(class: "new", gap: .sm) {
            Input(bind: draft, placeholder: "What needs doing?", aria-label: "New todo") {
                on key("Enter") { add() }
            }
            Button("Add", disabled: draft.trim() == "").primary {
                on click { add() }
            }
        }"#, title: "wf")

        Markdown("- `bind: draft` ties the input to the state both ways: typing changes `draft`, and `draft = \"\"` empties the box.\n- `query` is the address's query string as a value, kept current. So `filter` follows the address, and `shown` follows `filter`.\n- A `match` over an enum must cover every case. If you add a fourth case to `Filter`, this `match` is an error until it handles it.\n\nThe second half draws the filters and the list, and closes the page. Add it below the first, after a blank line:")

        CodeBlock(#"// src/pages/Home.wf
        Row(class: "filters", gap: .xs, align: .center) {
            Link("All", to: "/?show=all", class: { "is-on": filter == .all })
            Link("Open", to: "/?show=open", class: { "is-on": filter == .open })
            Link("Done", to: "/?show=done", class: { "is-on": filter == .done })
            Spacer
            if Todos.done.length > 0 {
                Button("Clear done").sm {
                    on click { Todos.clearDone() }
                }
            }
        }

        if shown.length == 0 {
            Text(if Todos.items.length == 0 { "Nothing yet — add your first todo above." } else { "Nothing here." }, class: "empty")
        }
        Stack(class: "list") {
            for todo in shown by todo.id {
                TodoRow(todo, animate: .fadeIn, exit: .fadeOut)
            }
        }
    }
    Text("Your list stays in this browser, and nowhere else.", class: "hint")
}"#, title: "wf")

        Markdown("- `for … by todo.id` is a keyed list. When a todo is renamed, or the filter hides it, only its row changes; the other rows keep their elements, and the row being edited keeps its cursor ([Control flow](/docs/guide/control-flow)).\n- `animate:` and `exit:` fade a row in and out.\n- A class map, `\{ \"is-on\": filter == .all \}`, turns a class on while its condition holds.\n\nLast, the `app` declaration is the frame every page sits in. `Router` marks where the current page is drawn:")

        CodeBlock(#"// src/App.wf
// The frame every page sits in: a narrow column, centred.
app {
    Container(class: "shell") {
        Router
    }
}"#, title: "wf")

        Markdown("Now start the development server in a second terminal, and leave it running. Every save rebuilds the project and reloads the page:")

        Terminal(lines: [
                Line(command: "wf serve")
            ])

        Markdown("**Check it:** `wf check` prints `No problems in todos.`, and <http://localhost:3000/> shows a card headed **Todos** with `0 left` and *Nothing yet — add your first todo above.* Type a todo and press Enter: it appears, and the count reads `1 left`. Reload the page, and the todo is still there. Click **Open**, and the address becomes `/?show=open`.\n\nIf the server prints `No theme Paper is declared in this project`, you probably skipped `src/theme.wf` in step 2. If a store member shows as `U04` here, you probably left out part of the page.")

        Heading("Step 7: Write tests", id: "step-7-write-tests").h2

        Markdown("A test draws what it declares, then follows its steps in order. It types into the control named **New todo** and clicks the button named **Add**, the way a reader would ([Testing](/docs/guide/testing)). Create `tests/todos.wf` with this test:")

        CodeBlock(#"// tests/todos.wf
test "adding a todo puts it in the list" {
    use Todos
    state draft = ""
    Input(bind: draft, aria-label: "New todo")
    Button("Add") { on click { Todos.add(draft)  draft = "" } }
    for todo in Todos.items by todo.id { TodoRow(todo) }
    Text("{Todos.open.length} left")

    expect "0 left"
    type "Buy bread" into "New todo"
    click "Add"
    expect "Buy bread"
    expect "1 left"
}"#, title: "wf")

        Markdown("A test that clicks or types runs in a headless Chrome. The finished project has six tests in [`tests/todos.wf`](https://github.com/monzeromer-lab/WebFluent/blob/master/examples/tutorials/easy-todos/tests/todos.wf): two that only look at a row, and four that click — adding a todo, refusing a blank one, ticking and clearing, and renaming that keeps one row for each. Copy the file to have them all, then run them:")

        Terminal(lines: [
                Line(command: "wf test")
            ])

        Markdown("**Check it:** with the whole file, `wf test` ends with `6 passed, 0 failed, 2 snapshot(s) written`. The two tests that only look write a snapshot of what they drew under `tests/__snapshots__/`, and later runs compare against it.\n\nIf a test that clicks reports that no browser was found, Chrome is not where `wf` looks: set `WF_CHROME` to its path.")

        Heading("Step 8: Build it", id: "step-8-build-it").h2

        Markdown("Check, test and build the project:")

        Terminal(lines: [
                Line(command: "wf check"),
                Line(command: "wf test"),
                Line(command: "wf build")
            ])

        Markdown("`wf check` reports every finding and writes nothing. `wf build` writes `build/`, which any static host serves — [Deploying](/docs/guide/deploying) covers GitHub Pages, Netlify and the rest. To load the built page in a real browser before you deploy, run `wf verify`: it fails on an error, a missing file or a page that draws nothing.\n\n**Check it:** `wf build` ends with `Build complete.`, and `build/` holds `index.html`, `app.js` and `styles.css`.")

        Heading("What you built", id: "what-you-built").h2

        Markdown("- A `type` and an `enum`, held to every use ([Types](/docs/guide/types)).\n- A store whose list survives a reload with `persist`, and `derived` values that follow it ([Stores](/docs/guide/stores)).\n- A component with state of its own, and accessible names on every control ([Components](/docs/guide/components)).\n- A keyed list, and a filter kept in the address with `query` ([Control flow](/docs/guide/control-flow)).\n- A theme with a dark variant, and the project's own stylesheet ([Styling](/docs/guide/styling)).\n- Tests that look and tests that click ([Testing](/docs/guide/testing)).")
    }
}
